SUSPECTED BUG: a typed nil returned through a helper with a pointer result type is silently dropped.
gateway.Precheck does return check(n); check returns *CodeError, nil for small n: converted to error this is
a NON-nil error holding a nil pointer, which if err != nil { return err } forwards (the app prints it).
Expected 2 entries: concrete *CodeError (the &CodeError literal in gateway.check) and concrete *CodeError
[typed nil] (the "return nil" in gateway.check). Actual: only the literal; no entry and no Unresolved for the
typed nil. (A function that only does "return nilPtrHelper()" gets "0 entries" although it never returns nil.)
